The legal texts come from TanzLII (Judiciary of Tanzania, on the Laws.Africa Peachjam platform):

  TanzLII, https://tanzlii.org, point-in-time versions of each act, read from archived copies of its
  pages on the Internet Archive (https://web.archive.org), retrieved 2026-10-28.

Licence and terms, as TanzLII states them: CC BY-NC 4.0, crediting TanzLII as the source (https://tanzlii.org/terms-of-use/).
CC BY-NC 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

Attribution:

  Source: TanzLII (https://tanzlii.org), a project of the Judiciary of Tanzania, licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0).

The texts may be used only for non-commercial purposes. This repository is private; whether and how it
may be published is the owner's decision under these terms.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per
line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; editorial notes, Part and Chapter headings were left out;
and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws TanzLII names for each change.
The wording of the law was not changed. Neither TanzLII nor Laws.Africa endorses this repository.

<!-- acts:start -->
Acts of Parliament in the folders act-YYYY-NNN/: copies of Acts of the Parliament of the United Republic of
Tanzania as passed, from the Parliament of Tanzania's Acts list (https://polis.bunge.go.tz/), retrieved 2026-11-03.
The site states no licence or terms of use. The Copyright and Neighbouring Rights Act (Cap. 218), section 7, gives
no protection to laws. The texts are reproduced without change to their wording. Neither the Parliament of
Tanzania nor the Government Printer endorses this repository.
<!-- acts:end -->

